\paragraph{Impact on genuine-rate comparison.}
After H8 reclassification and H7 false-negative correction: ISR genuine $= 14/231 = 6.1\%$ vs.\ random genuine $= 25/262 = 9.5\%$ (Fisher $p{=}0.182$, n.s.; Wilson 95\% CI: ISR [3.6\%, 9.9\%], Random [6.5\%, 13.7\%]).
The direction is consistent with ISR-specific gaming modes displacing genuine output, but the effect is not statistically significant at the conventional $\alpha{=}0.05$ threshold.

